   "source": [
    "# **LASSO Feature Selection — Diabetes**\n",
    "\n",
    "## **Overall Interpretation**\n",
    "\n",
    "The LASSO experiment evaluated conventional LASSO feature selection against **LASSO + Rank Fusion DODA**, using Logistic Regression, Random Forest, and XGBoost across Top-5, Top-10, Top-15, and Top-20 feature subsets.\n",
    "\n",
    "The Diabetes dataset contains 21 candidate features, and the LASSO baseline was implemented using **L1-regularized Logistic Regression with C = 0.1**. DODA subsequently combined the LASSO-derived mathematical ranking with clinically informed feature weights using **Rank Fusion**.\n",
    "\n",
    "The results show that DODA does **not uniformly improve predictive performance across all models and feature budgets**. Instead, its main contribution is the refinement of the LASSO feature ranking using clinical information while retaining the strongest statistically supported features.\n",
    "\n",
    "The most consistent feature core across the experiment consisted of:\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, Age, HighBP, HighChol`\n",
    "\n",
    "These five features formed the complete Top-5 subset for both LASSO and DODA across the repeated evaluation runs.\n",
    "\n",
    "At larger feature budgets, DODA increasingly modified the composition of the selected feature subsets, particularly by introducing clinically emphasized variables such as `DiffWalk`, `PhysHlth`, and `Stroke`.\n",
    "\n",
    "The repeated evaluation therefore suggests that DODA primarily functions as a **clinically guided re-ranking mechanism**, with its predictive effect depending on both the downstream model and the number of selected features.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## **1. LASSO Baseline Feature Selection**\n",
    "\n",
    "The LASSO baseline consistently prioritised a core group of diabetes-related features.\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-5, the selected features were:\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, Age, HighBP, HighChol`\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-10, the feature set expanded to:\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, Age, HighBP, HighChol, CholCheck, HvyAlcoholConsump, Sex, Income, HeartDiseaseorAttack`\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-15, LASSO additionally included:\n",
    "\n",
    "`PhysHlth, DiffWalk, MentHlth, Stroke, AnyHealthcare`\n",
    "\n",
    "The Top-20 configuration retained 20 of the 21 available predictors, adding:\n",
    "\n",
    "`Education, Fruits, Smoker, PhysActivity, Veggies`\n",
    "\n",
    "while `NoDocbcCost` remained outside the Top-20 subset.\n",
    "\n",
    "This indicates that LASSO consistently placed `GenHlth`, `BMI`, `Age`, `HighBP`, and `HighChol` at the center of the statistical ranking.\n",
    "\n",
    "The repeated selection results further support this observation, with the Top-5 LASSO subset remaining identical across all 25 repeated runs.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## **2. Effect of Rank Fusion DODA on Feature Selection**\n",
    "\n",
    "After applying Rank Fusion DODA, the Top-5 feature set remained unchanged:\n",
    "\n",
    "**LASSO:**\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, Age, HighBP, HighChol`\n",
    "\n",
    "**LASSO + DODA:**\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, HighBP, Age, HighChol`\n",
    "\n",
    "The difference at Top-5 was therefore only an ordering change rather than a change in feature membership.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is an important result because it shows that the clinical ranking did not displace the strongest LASSO-selected features.\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-10, however, DODA produced a more meaningful change.\n",
    "\n",
    "**LASSO Top-10:**\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, Age, HighBP, HighChol, CholCheck, HvyAlcoholConsump, Sex, Income, HeartDiseaseorAttack`\n",
    "\n",
    "**DODA Top-10:**\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, HighBP, Age, HighChol, HeartDiseaseorAttack, CholCheck, DiffWalk, PhysHlth, Stroke`\n",
    "\n",
    "Thus, DODA retained the major statistical core while replacing:\n",
    "\n",
    "`HvyAlcoholConsump, Sex, Income`\n",
    "\n",
    "with:\n",
    "\n",
    "`DiffWalk, PhysHlth, Stroke`\n",
    "\n",
    "This represents a shift from socioeconomic and behavioral variables toward additional clinical and functional-health variables.\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-15, DODA selected:\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, HighBP, Age, HighChol, HeartDiseaseorAttack, CholCheck, PhysHlth, DiffWalk, Stroke, HvyAlcoholConsump, Income, Sex, MentHlth, Smoker`\n",
    "\n",
    "Compared with the LASSO Top-15 subset, the main membership change was the inclusion of `Smoker` and exclusion of `AnyHealthcare`.\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-20, the LASSO and DODA subsets were identical:\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, HighBP, Age, HighChol, HeartDiseaseorAttack, CholCheck, PhysHlth, DiffWalk, Stroke, HvyAlcoholConsump, Income, Sex, MentHlth, Smoker, Education, AnyHealthcare, PhysActivity, Fruits, Veggies`\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, the effect of DODA was strongest in the intermediate feature budgets, particularly Top-10 and Top-15, while the feature-space difference disappeared at Top-20.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## **3. Top-5 Predictive Performance**\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-5, DODA produced almost no feature-space change because both methods selected the same five features.\n",
    "\n",
    "The repeated evaluation therefore provides a useful baseline for determining whether Rank Fusion changes downstream performance even when the selected feature set remains identical.\n",
    "\n",
    "The overall Diabetes benchmark reports that, across the complete 120-run Diabetes experiment, DODA produced only a very small change in average predictive performance compared with the baseline.\n",
    "\n",
    "For the LASSO method specifically, the reported macro-averaged changes were:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Accuracy: **−0.0003**\n",
    "* Precision: **+0.0001**\n",
    "* Recall: **+0.0025**\n",
    "* F1-score: **+0.0011**\n",
    "\n",
    "These changes indicate that DODA produced only a small overall predictive shift for LASSO while slightly increasing recall and F1-score.\n",
    "\n",
    "The Top-5 feature set itself was completely preserved, indicating that the clinical information primarily affected ranking rather than replacing the statistically dominant predictors.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## **4. Top-10 Predictive Performance**\n",
    "\n",
    "Top-10 represents the point at which DODA produced one of the clearest changes in feature composition.\n",
    "\n",
    "The LASSO subset contained:\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, Age, HighBP, HighChol, CholCheck, HvyAlcoholConsump, Sex, Income, HeartDiseaseorAttack`\n",
    "\n",
    "whereas DODA selected:\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, HighBP, Age, HighChol, HeartDiseaseorAttack, CholCheck, DiffWalk, PhysHlth, Stroke`\n",
    "\n",
    "Three features from the LASSO subset:\n",
    "\n",
    "`HvyAlcoholConsump, Sex, Income`\n",
    "\n",
    "were replaced by:\n",
    "\n",
    "`DiffWalk, PhysHlth, Stroke`\n",
    "\n",
    "This indicates that Rank Fusion incorporated the configured clinical importance into the feature ranking while retaining the strongest LASSO features.\n",
    "\n",
    "The overall Diabetes benchmark shows that the predictive effect of DODA remained small when averaged across all feature-selection methods and classifiers. Across the complete experiment, DODA changed mean accuracy from **0.7383 to 0.7376**, while recall increased from **0.6145 to 0.6213**, and F1-score increased from **0.3957 to 0.3992**.\n",
    "\n",
    "For LASSO specifically, the corresponding change was:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Accuracy: **−0.0003**\n",
    "* Precision: **+0.0001**\n",
    "* Recall: **+0.0025**\n",
    "* F1-score: **+0.0011**\n",
    "\n",
    "Thus, the Top-10 feature substitution should not be interpreted as proof that the replacement variables are independently superior predictors. Instead, it demonstrates that DODA can modify the feature composition while maintaining broadly comparable predictive behavior.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## **5. Top-15 Predictive Performance**\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-15, DODA continued to retain the dominant statistical feature core:\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, HighBP, Age, HighChol`\n",
    "\n",
    "while incorporating additional clinically relevant variables.\n",
    "\n",
    "The LASSO Top-15 subset included:\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, Age, HighBP, HighChol, CholCheck, HvyAlcoholConsump, Sex, Income, HeartDiseaseorAttack, PhysHlth, DiffWalk, MentHlth, Stroke, AnyHealthcare`\n",
    "\n",
    "DODA selected:\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, HighBP, Age, HighChol, HeartDiseaseorAttack, CholCheck, PhysHlth, DiffWalk, Stroke, HvyAlcoholConsump, Income, Sex, MentHlth, Smoker`\n",
    "\n",
    "The main change was therefore:\n",
    "\n",
    "`AnyHealthcare → Smoker`\n",
    "\n",
    "while the remaining 14 features were retained.\n",
    "\n",
    "This represents a relatively modest modification compared with Top-10.\n",
    "\n",
    "The repeated feature-selection results also show that DODA maintained high stability at Top-15, with a mean Jaccard similarity of **0.9725** across the 25 repeated runs.\n",
    "\n",
    "Thus, although the feature composition differs slightly from LASSO, the DODA-selected Top-15 subsets remained highly consistent across repeated evaluations.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## **6. Top-20 Predictive Performance**\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-20, the LASSO and DODA feature sets became identical.\n",
    "\n",
    "The selected feature set was:\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, HighBP, Age, HighChol, HeartDiseaseorAttack, CholCheck, PhysHlth, DiffWalk, Stroke, HvyAlcoholConsump, Income, Sex, MentHlth, Smoker, Education, AnyHealthcare, PhysActivity, Fruits, Veggies`\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, at Top-20 there is no feature-membership difference between the two approaches.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is useful as a reference condition because any difference between LASSO and DODA at smaller Top-K values cannot be attributed simply to the number of predictors available.\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-20, the repeated stability results also converged:\n",
    "\n",
    "* LASSO mean Jaccard: **0.9733**\n",
    "* DODA mean Jaccard: **0.9733**\n",
    "\n",
    "Both methods therefore produced the same level of feature-set stability when almost the entire feature space was retained.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## **7. Repeated Cross-Validation Results**\n",
    "\n",
    "The experiment used **5-fold Repeated Stratified Cross-Validation with 5 repeats**, producing **25 repeated train-test evaluations**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Across the complete Diabetes benchmark, the macro-averaged results were:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Metric    | Baseline |   DODA |  Change |\n",
    "| --------- | -------: | -----: | ------: |\n",
    "| Accuracy  |   0.7383 | 0.7376 | −0.0007 |\n",
    "| Precision |   0.3327 | 0.3320 | −0.0007 |\n",
    "| Recall    |   0.6145 | 0.6213 | +0.0068 |\n",
    "| F1-score  |   0.3957 | 0.3992 | +0.0035 |\n",
    "| ROC-AUC   |   0.7894 | 0.7897 | +0.0003 |\n",
    "\n",
    "These results indicate that DODA maintained essentially comparable overall discrimination while producing a modest increase in recall and F1-score.\n",
    "\n",
    "For the **LASSO method specifically**, the reported changes were:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Metric    | Change with DODA |\n",
    "| --------- | ---------------: |\n",
    "| Accuracy  |          −0.0003 |\n",
    "| Precision |          +0.0001 |\n",
    "| Recall    |          +0.0025 |\n",
    "| F1-score  |          +0.0011 |\n",
    "\n",
    "The magnitude of these changes is small, indicating that Rank Fusion DODA did not dramatically alter the predictive behavior of LASSO.\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead, the main observable contribution was the modification of feature composition.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## **8. Feature-Selection Stability**\n",
    "\n",
    "Feature-selection stability is one of the strongest findings of the Diabetes LASSO experiment.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Top-K | LASSO Mean Jaccard | DODA Mean Jaccard | DODA SD |\n",
    "| ----: | -----------------: | ----------------: | ------: |\n",
    "|     5 |         **1.0000** |        **1.0000** |  0.0000 |\n",
    "|    10 |             0.9067 |        **0.9855** |  0.0494 |\n",
    "|    15 |             0.9259 |        **0.9725** |  0.0519 |\n",
    "|    20 |         **0.9733** |        **0.9733** |  0.0428 |\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-5, both methods achieved complete stability, with a mean Jaccard similarity of **1.0000**.\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-10, DODA showed a particularly clear stability advantage:\n",
    "\n",
    "**LASSO:** 0.9067\n",
    "\n",
    "**DODA:** 0.9855\n",
    "\n",
    "This represents a substantially more consistent feature subset across the repeated runs.\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-15, DODA also maintained higher stability:\n",
    "\n",
    "**LASSO:** 0.9259\n",
    "\n",
    "**DODA:** 0.9725\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-20, both methods achieved the same mean Jaccard value of **0.9733**, consistent with the fact that their selected feature sets were identical.\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, the stability results suggest that the contribution of DODA is particularly visible when the feature budget is restricted to an intermediate number of predictors.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## **9. Feature Selection Frequency**\n",
    "\n",
    "The feature-selection frequency analysis further supports the stability of the DODA Top-5 subset.\n",
    "\n",
    "For DODA Top-5, all five features were selected in **25/25 repeated runs**:\n",
    "\n",
    "* `Age`: **100%**\n",
    "* `BMI`: **100%**\n",
    "* `GenHlth`: **100%**\n",
    "* `HighBP`: **100%**\n",
    "* `HighChol`: **100%**\n",
    "\n",
    "Thus, the same five-feature clinical-statistical core was reproduced throughout the repeated evaluation.\n",
    "\n",
    "The LASSO Top-5 subset was also selected identically across all 25 runs.\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-10 and Top-15, the feature sets showed somewhat more variation, which is expected because additional lower-ranked features compete for the remaining feature positions.\n",
    "\n",
    "Nevertheless, DODA maintained high overall subset stability, particularly at Top-10 and Top-15.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## **10. LASSO vs. DODA Feature-Set Agreement**\n",
    "\n",
    "The direct comparison between LASSO and DODA provides an additional view of how strongly Rank Fusion modifies the feature space.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Top-K | Same Feature Set | Mean Jaccard Agreement | Mean Common Features |\n",
    "| ----: | ---------------: | ---------------------: | -------------------: |\n",
    "|     5 |         **100%** |             **1.0000** |                 5.00 |\n",
    "|    10 |           **0%** |                 0.5436 |                 7.04 |\n",
    "|    15 |               4% |                 0.8756 |                14.00 |\n",
    "|    20 |         **100%** |             **1.0000** |                20.00 |\n",
    "\n",
    "The Top-5 result shows complete agreement between the two methods.\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-10, none of the 25 repeated runs produced exactly the same feature set, and the mean Jaccard agreement was **0.5436**, indicating substantial feature-space modification.\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-15, the two approaches shared an average of **14 out of 15 features**, producing a much higher mean Jaccard agreement of **0.8756**.\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-20, the feature sets were identical in all 25 runs.\n",
    "\n",
    "This demonstrates that DODA's effect is strongest at the intermediate Top-10 feature budget, while the difference naturally disappears as the feature budget approaches the full feature space.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## **11. Clinical Interpretation of the Feature Changes**\n",
    "\n",
    "The DODA ranking demonstrates a consistent tendency to preserve the strongest statistical predictors while incorporating variables assigned greater clinical importance.\n",
    "\n",
    "The core retained features were:\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, Age, HighBP, HighChol`\n",
    "\n",
    "These features remained dominant in both LASSO and DODA.\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-10, DODA replaced:\n",
    "\n",
    "`HvyAlcoholConsump, Sex, Income`\n",
    "\n",
    "with:\n",
    "\n",
    "`DiffWalk, PhysHlth, Stroke`\n",
    "\n",
    "This represents a shift toward additional health-status, functional, and disease-related variables within the selected feature space.\n",
    "\n",
    "The change should be interpreted as a **ranking and feature-composition effect**, rather than evidence that the DODA-selected variables are independently superior predictors.\n",
    "\n",
    "The mathematical LASSO score and the clinical weighting mechanism represent different sources of information. DODA combines them through Rank Fusion, meaning that a feature can move upward because of its combined statistical and clinical ranking rather than because its independent predictive contribution increased.\n",
    "\n",
    "This distinction is particularly important when interpreting the feature-selection results in a clinical ML study.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## **12. Overall Interpretation**\n",
    "\n",
    "The Diabetes LASSO experiment demonstrates that **Rank Fusion DODA modifies the LASSO feature composition while preserving a highly stable statistical core**.\n",
    "\n",
    "The most consistently selected features were:\n",
    "\n",
    "`GenHlth, BMI, Age, HighBP, HighChol`\n",
    "\n",
    "These five features were selected in **25/25 repeated runs** by DODA at Top-5, producing a mean Jaccard similarity of **1.0000**.\n",
    "\n",
    "The effect of DODA became more visible at Top-10, where it replaced three LASSO-selected variables:\n",
    "\n",
    "`HvyAlcoholConsump, Sex, Income`\n",
    "\n",
    "with:\n",
    "\n",
    "`DiffWalk, PhysHlth, Stroke`\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-15, the modification was smaller, with DODA replacing `AnyHealthcare` with `Smoker`.\n",
    "\n",
    "At Top-20, the two approaches selected the same 20-feature subset.\n",
    "\n",
    "The stability analysis provides particularly strong evidence for the reproducibility of the DODA rankings. DODA achieved higher mean Jaccard similarity than LASSO at both Top-10 (**0.9855 vs. 0.9067**) and Top-15 (**0.9725 vs. 0.9259**), while both approaches achieved complete stability at Top-5 and identical stability at Top-20.\n",
    "\n",
    "Predictively, DODA did **not produce a universal performance improvement**. Across the complete Diabetes benchmark, DODA produced nearly unchanged accuracy and ROC-AUC while slightly increasing recall and F1-score. For the LASSO method specifically, the changes were small: accuracy decreased by **0.0003**, while recall increased by **0.0025** and F1-score by **0.0011**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, the Diabetes results support the interpretation of DODA as a **clinically guided re-ranking mechanism rather than a universal predictive-performance optimizer**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Its main contribution is the ability to incorporate clinical information into the statistical feature-selection process while retaining the strongest LASSO-derived predictors and producing highly reproducible feature subsets.\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall, the experiment demonstrates that Rank Fusion DODA can provide a more clinically structured feature space without substantially changing the predictive behavior of the underlying LASSO-based selection process. The strongest evidence is observed in the **stable Top-5 core and the increased stability of the Top-10 and Top-15 feature subsets**, while the predictive results indicate that the value of DODA should be assessed jointly through **feature composition, stability, and predictive performance**, rather than accuracy or ROC-AUC alone.\n"
   ]
